<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the notarized Flow.app. dist.sh signs with
  the hardened runtime enabled, so this file is the app's entire resource
  access story.

  It was empty until #469, on the reasoning that Keychain and UserNotifications
  need no entitlement under the hardened runtime. True when it was written, and
  then huddles added mic and camera and nobody came back here. The hardened
  runtime refuses those two before TCC is ever consulted: no consent prompt, no
  row in Privacy & Security, and AVCaptureDevice.requestAccess returning false
  in four milliseconds. Every released build had it and no local build did,
  because make-app.sh signs without the hardened runtime, which is why it took
  a report from someone else's machine to find.

  Measured on the release cert, hardened runtime, varying only this file:
    empty file        notDetermined, requestAccess false in 0.004s, then denied
    with audio-input  notDetermined, prompt shown, then authorized

  Keep this minimal: one key per capability Flow actually uses, and only once
  the runtime proves it needs it. Do NOT enable App Sandbox here.

  Note for editors: this file is parsed by AMFI, whose XML parser rejects a
  double hyphen inside a comment. Spell flags out in words.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Huddle mic. Without this the hardened runtime denies capture outright. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Huddle video (#435). Same gate, same failure mode. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
